yle=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;\"> 9 12 25 26 32 19<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(31,78,121)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(192,0,0)\">#now construct the scrFrame (which works):<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(31,78,121)\">sf &lt;- data2oscr(edf = r1, tdf = list(rbs.tdf1),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(31,78,121)\">                sess.col = 1, id.col = 2, occ.col = 3, trap.col = 4,<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(31,78,121)\">                K = 7, ntraps=nrow(rbs.tdf1))$scrFrame<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(31,78,121)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(31,78,121)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(192,0,0)\">#and now examining the caphist object we see no detections in occasion 4:<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(31,78,121)\">apply(sf$caphist[[1]],c(3),sum)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;\">[1]  9 12 25  0 26 32 19<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Garamond,serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Garamond,serif;color:black\">All this is to say that there is a different issue. Are you sure you have provided the right value of </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(68,114,196)\">K</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Garamond,serif;color:black\">?<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Garamond,serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Garamond,serif;color:black\">Chris<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Garamond,serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><div style=\"border-right:none;border-bottom:none;border-left:none;border-top:1pt solid rgb(225,225,225);padding:3pt 0cm 0cm\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\">From:</span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_p...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_p...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; <b>On Behalf Of </b>Joël W. Jameson<br><b>Sent:</b> 22 September 2021 19:04<br><b>To:</b> oSCR &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_p...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br><b>Subject:</b> [oscr] Occasions with no captures<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hello,<u></u><u></u></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am getting the following error &quot;some occassion names in EDF not in TDF&quot; when running  data2oscr on multisession data. I do not get this error when I have captures on every occasion. However, I get the error when I include a session for which I am missing data (no captures) for some occasions. For example, the occasion column would look like this: 11111222233336666... This leads me to believe that the error occurs because I am missing lines for some occasions.<u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">How can I integrate occasions with no captures in the data so as to not receive the error?<u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thank you<u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Joel<u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">-- <br>You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;oSCR&quot; group.<br>To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_package...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>To view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/oscr_package/b741fc37-75f0-4ba1-9267-c5209a01a2a6n%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/oscr_package/b741fc37-75f0-4ba1-9267-c5209a01a2a6n%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492030973000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1n1ezUb0lJUZIzrrg-vORH\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/oscr_package/b741fc37-75f0-4ba1-9267-c5209a01a2a6n%40googlegroups.com</a>.<u></u><u></u></p></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br></blockquote></div>"
